== en
titulo: Grandparents, uncles and cousins
intro: Learn vocabulary for the extended family and marital status with estar: casado, soltero, abuelos, tíos, primos, and nietos.
b1.titulo: The wider family and marital status
b1.texto: "The masculine plural covers both genders: **los abuelos** are grandfather and grandmother, **los tíos** uncle and aunt, and **los hijos** sons and daughters.\n\nIn Spanish we use **de** to indicate family relationships: *el padre de mi madre es mi abuelo*.\n\nTo talk about marital status we usually use the verb **estar** with adjectives agreeing in gender: **estoy casado / casada**, **está soltero / soltera**.\n\nTo ask questions we say: *¿Estás casado?*, *¿Tienes hijos?*. And reply: *Tengo dos hijos: un hijo y una hija*.\n\nFor relative age we use **mayor** (older) and **menor** (younger): *mi hermano mayor*."
b2.titulo: Are you married?
b2.f0.texto: Are you married?
b2.f1.texto: No, I am single.
b2.f2.texto: My husband is called Marcos.
b2.f3.texto: We have two children.
b2.f4.texto: My grandparents have ten grandchildren.
b2.f5.texto: I have many cousins.
b3.titulo: Vocabulary
b4.titulo: Marital status with estar
b4.texto: "The marital status adjective agrees with the person we are speaking about:\n\n- **Masculine**: Pablo está casado.\n- **Feminine**: Lucía está casada.\n\nUse *soltero / soltera* for people who are not married."
b4.e0.texto: Pablo is married.
b4.e1.texto: Lucía is married.
b5.titulo: In the grandparents' village
b5.f0.texto: Pablo's lovely grandparents live in a truly picturesque and pleasant village.
b5.f1.texto: They own a very large stone house surrounded by tall green leafy trees.
b5.f2.texto: The entire family gathers together every summer with immense heartfelt joy.
b5.f3.texto: My uncles are extraordinarily friendly and have two cheerful, playful children.
b5.f4.texto: My cousins always play happily together across the spacious green garden lawn.
b5.f5.texto: All of us gladly share the hearty homemade meal around the long table.
b6.titulo: Which option is correct?
b6.pregunta: Your mother's brother is your…?
b6.o0: tío
b6.o0.refuerzo: Correct: your mother's or father's brother is your uncle (tío).
b6.o1: primo
b6.o1.refuerzo: Incorrect: your uncle's son is your cousin (primo).
b6.o2: abuelo
b6.o2.refuerzo: Incorrect: your parents' father is your grandfather (abuelo).
b7.titulo: Fill in the blank
b7.pregunta: Complete the sentence with the correct word.
b7.frase: Los padres de mi padre son mis ___.
b7.o0: abuelos
b7.o0.refuerzo: Correct: your father's parents are your grandparents (abuelos).
b7.o1: tíos
b7.o1.refuerzo: Incorrect: tíos are uncles and aunts.
b7.o2: nietos
b7.o2.refuerzo: Incorrect: nietos are grandchildren.
b8.titulo: Put the words in order
b8.frase: Tengo dos hijos.
b8.traduccion: I have two children.
b9.titulo: Write the sentence
b9.pregunta: Write in Spanish: «I have two children».
